    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You\u2019re a circle. Everything else wants you gone.<br>But every time you die, you leave something behind \u2014 a glowing shield, a permanent upgrade, a memory of failure turned into a tool for survival.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Die. Upgrade. Try again.</strong><br>In this neon-lit bullet hell, every death creates a persistent upgrade that stays on the battlefield \u2014 blocking bullets, shaping new strategies, and gradually turning chaos into rhythm.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a small, free game I made during a game jam.<br>I liked the vibe, so I decided to polish it up and share it here on Steam. It\u2019s short, weird, and (hopefully) satisfying. No microtransactions, no fluff \u2014 just you, the shapes, and the bullets.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You\u2019re a circle. Everything else wants you gone.<br>But every time you die, you leave something behind \u2014 a glowing shield, a permanent upgrade, a memory of failure turned into a tool for survival.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Die. Upgrade. Try again.</strong><br>In this neon-lit bullet hell, every death creates a persistent upgrade that stays on the battlefield \u2014 blocking bullets, shaping new strategies, and gradually turning chaos into rhythm.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a small, free game I made during a game jam.<br>I liked the vibe, so I decided to polish it up and share it here on Steam. It\u2019s short, weird, and (hopefully) satisfying. No microtransactions, no fluff \u2014 just you, the shapes, and the bullets.</p>",
    "short_description": "A fast-paced, minimalist bullet hell where dying makes you stronger. Originally made for a game jam, now polished and released as a free standalone.",
